1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,514
When deploying generative AI into modern columnar data warehouses,

2
00:00:05,514 --> 00:00:09,285
the most dangerous bugs aren't syntax errors.

3
00:00:09,285 --> 00:00:13,326
It is when a query executes without a single warning,

4
00:00:13,326 --> 00:00:18,984
but silently quadruples your financial KPIs or corrupts user cohorts.

5
00:00:18,984 --> 00:00:25,045
Traditional benchmarks only test basic relational lookups and textbook joins.

6
00:00:25,045 --> 00:00:32,049
We built SQL Frontier Eval to evaluate frontier models on real-world analytical invariants.

7
00:00:32,849 --> 00:00:39,213
To truly stress-test frontier models, we curated an eight-category failure taxonomy.

8
00:00:39,213 --> 00:00:44,250
This covers high-stakes real-world pitfalls like the Chasm Trap,

9
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:50,216
where joining two one-to-many child tables multiplies gross revenue four-fold.

10
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:56,182
We test Gaps and Islands sessionization with thirty-minute inactivity thresholds,

11
00:00:56,182 --> 00:01:01,485
point-in-time SCD Type Two joins with open-ended null bounds,

12
00:01:01,485 --> 00:01:08,776
and subtle three-valued logic where a single NULL in a subquery empties an entire dataset.

13
00:01:08,776 --> 00:01:15,670
We also evaluate window frame bounds, funnel precedence, and non-SARGable date pruning.

14
00:01:16,469 --> 00:01:23,424
Under the hood, SQL Frontier Eval executes inside an isolated in-memory DuckDB sandbox.

15
00:01:23,424 --> 00:01:29,682
To eliminate test flakiness, our grader enforces deterministic multiset row sorting.

16
00:01:29,682 --> 00:01:34,967
Crucially, our engine inspects DuckDB's physical EXPLAIN plan

17
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:41,643
to flag disallowed anti-patterns like Cartesian cross products and quadratic joins.

18
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:48,597
And whenever an evaluation fails, the harness automatically generates a full walkthrough

19
00:01:48,597 --> 00:01:55,829
displaying side-by-side output tables, arithmetic deltas, and root-cause explanations.

20
00:01:56,629 --> 00:02:03,792
We evaluated frontier models across major AI providers: Gemini, Claude, and GPT.

21
00:02:03,792 --> 00:02:09,236
The empirical scorecard revealed significant capability differences.

22
00:02:09,236 --> 00:02:15,682
Gemini 3.8 Flash with Medium Reasoning achieved a perfect eight out of eight,

23
00:02:15,682 --> 00:02:19,264
flawlessly handling every analytical trap.

24
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:26,140
Claude Opus 4.6 Thinking, Claude Sonnet 4.6, GPT-OSS 120B, and Gemini Low

25
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:31,583
all delivered fast inference and scored seven out of eight,

26
00:02:31,583 --> 00:02:38,459
with all of them failing on Task 06: strict sequential funnel precedence.

27
00:02:39,259 --> 00:02:44,969
Here is why Task 06 was the great discriminator between frontier models.

28
00:02:44,969 --> 00:02:50,135
When calculating sequential user onboarding conversion stages,

29
00:02:50,135 --> 00:02:55,845
Claude and GPT wrote multiple unnested distinct count subqueries.

30
00:02:55,845 --> 00:03:01,962
This triggered internal Cartesian cross-product execution plans in DuckDB.

31
00:03:01,962 --> 00:03:08,760
In contrast, Gemini 3.8 Flash with Medium Reasoning synthesized a single-scan CTE

32
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:14,469
using conditional aggregation flags that executed in just four milliseconds.

33
00:03:15,269 --> 00:03:21,176
SQL Frontier Eval is fully reproducible and packaged for hackathon submission.

34
00:03:21,176 --> 00:03:27,476
The entire codebase is compressed into an eighty-seven kilobyte code-only archive.

35
00:03:27,476 --> 00:03:34,301
A single script, verify dot s h, executes all twelve unit tests and baselines in five seconds.

36
00:03:34,301 --> 00:03:39,551
All empirical run logs are openly committed to the Git repository.

37
00:03:39,551 --> 00:03:46,769
This evaluation suite was developed using Google Antigravity with human engineering oversight.

38
00:03:46,769 --> 00:03:53,069
Thank you, and let us make AI data engineering reliable and mathematically sound.
